    "title": "TransDigm · historical macro and ESG review",
    "question": "Which rate, hedge and ESG cash-risk claims are supported, and what cannot yet be quantified?",
    "scope": "Historical consolidated TDG, September 30, 2024/FY2024 base, USD millions. Later December-quarter context is separately dated. All nine macro and eight ESG registers remain in the full analytical module page/Evidence; selected overview tables use the existing report design. Source-reported approximately30 interest sensitivity, arithmetic gross91.89 and conditional cash illustration are different measures. Neither a complete net hedge/FX/cost sensitivity nor financing outcome is established. Forward-starting collars were not active at the base. Recorded remediation41 is not incremental stress loss or payment evidence; missing sustainability-linked terms, pricing and target assurance remain gaps. The issuer’s contrary cost expectation is preserved. CP-2F is an alias request dispatched once as CP-2E. Supplemental handoffs are frozen context, not newly launched native heads. Retained-response replay, not fresh model/provider/native acceptance. Excel is ingestion-only; no workbook output."
